{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_eyzcm2klca","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll ask three clarifying questions one at a time to nail down the design, then write the plan.\n\nHow should sandwich ingredients, inventory, and allergens be modeled?\n\n- Fixed catalog with allergen tags: A hardcoded dict of ingredients (breads, proteins, cheeses, veggies, condiments), each with a quantity/stock count and a set of allergen tags (gluten, dairy, nuts, etc). Building a sandwich decrements stock; adding ingredients with conflicting allergens triggers a warning.\n- Simple catalog, no stock tracking: A fixed list of available ingredients with allergen tags, but no quantity/stock limits — any ingredient can be used any number of times. Simpler, focuses purely on allergen warnings.\n- User-defined inventory at runtime: No hardcoded catalog; users add their own ingredients (name, allergens, stock count) via CLI commands before building sandwiches. More flexible but more commands to implement/test.\n- Layered pantry inventory with substitutions and allergen exclusions (Book Recommended): Captured learner-authored choice.\n\nReply with one option per question."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dffc7ba-73cc-48ea-a264-5441b05533bc","uuid":"0d427f7b-278f-4175-a19b-4ac962377dfd","timestamp":"2026-08-30T22:02:05.710Z"}
