{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_a0ns7sawa6","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How should the CLI present command output (e.g., listing inventory, building a sandwich, showing warnings)?\n\n- Plain formatted text with sections: Human-readable text output using headers, indentation, and bullet-style lines (e.g., 'Sandwich built:' followed by ingredient list, then a 'Warnings:' section for substitutions/allergens). Easy to read in a terminal, no extra parsing needed.\n- Table-style output: Use fixed-width columns/tables (built with str.format/textwrap from the standard library) for listing inventory and receipts, giving a more structured, spreadsheet-like look.\n- JSON output: All command output is emitted as JSON (via the json module), making it machine-readable/scriptable at the cost of being less friendly to read directly in a terminal.\n- Assembly timeline plus a consolidated grocery list (Book Recommended): Captured learner-authored choice.\n\nReply with one option per question."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dffc7ba-73cc-48ea-a264-5441b05533bc","uuid":"669286fb-c5da-4fab-b730-a735648eea2f","timestamp":"2026-08-30T22:02:05.735Z"}
