{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_0xa1bkvt8f","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How should the app persist data between runs (inventory levels, order history, etc.)?\n\n- JSON file on disk: State (inventory stock, sandwich history) is loaded from and saved to a local JSON file (e.g., sandwich_data.json) using the json module. Simple, human-readable, easy to inspect/edit by hand.\n- No persistence (in-memory only): State resets every time the CLI is run; each invocation starts from the same default inventory. Simplest option, no file I/O to test, but stock/history don't carry over between runs.\n- SQLite database: State is stored in a local SQLite database file using the built-in sqlite3 module, giving structured querying and better handling of concurrent/larger data at the cost of more setup code.\n- Named sandwich profiles stored in a single JSON file (Book Recommended): Captured learner-authored choice.\n\nReply with one option per question."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dffc7ba-73cc-48ea-a264-5441b05533bc","uuid":"40449a9f-0d48-462d-a9d7-ca5eaed96ec2","timestamp":"2026-08-30T22:02:05.749Z"}
